==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-make a mountain out of a molehill.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{infl|en|verb|head=[[to]] [[make]] [[a]] [[mountain]] [[out]] [[of]] [[a]] [[molehill]]}}

# {{idiom}} To treat a [[problem]] as greater than it is; to [[blow something out of proportion]]; to [[exaggerate]] the [[importance]] of something [[trivial]]
#: ''If you're stuck in traffic, try not to '''make a mountain out of a molehill''' worrying about it too much. It could be much worse.''

